  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜ために: in order to (with an aim)",
     "texto": [
      "With a dictionary-form verb + **ために**, you state the aim of an action: **にほんご を はなす ため に、 まいにち べんきょう します** (I study every day in order to speak Japanese).",
      "The sentence usually continues with the action carried out to achieve that aim: **ためにです** doesn't work here as a complete answer."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "ために with nouns",
     "texto": [
      "If you express who something is for or what it is for, use **noun + のために**: **かぞく の ため に はたらきます** (I work for my family). With verbs, don't add の: **はなす ために**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Careful with «ため» and «のに»",
     "texto": [
      "**ため に** explains the purpose: in order to achieve something.",
      "Don't confuse it with **〜のに** (although), which you'll see in chapter 20."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
